// Regression: a tuplet on ONE staff must not reach another staff's beaming.
// Upper staff has a quarter-note triplet; lower staff has eight straight eighths
// that must beam 4+4. The beam pass once broke at a tuplet boundary BY NOTE INDEX,
// so the upper triplet's end-index split the lower staff's first group ([c d] +
// two stray flags + [g a b c']); tuplets carry a StaffIndex and the pass filters
// by it. ⚠️ The boundary rule itself was an invention and is gone (2026-07-31) —
// the filter now feeds only the beamlet clamp at a tuplet's own ends, and the
// lower staff's 4+4 comes from its own eighths against 4/4's beamExceptions.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/auto-beam-engraver.cc — beaming is per Voice/Staff context.
octave absolute
title "Multi-staff tuplet + beams"
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
section S {
  rh { tuplet 3/2 { c''4 c'' c'' } c''2 | }
  lh { c8 d e f g a b c' | }
}
form main { S }
score main "multistaff-tuplet-beams" { grandStaff { staff rh staff lh } }
